{%- comment -%}
  How many GARMENTS are in the bag.

  `cart.item_count` counts cart LINES times quantity, and a bundle is one line
  however many pieces it contains — so a two-garment set read BAG [1] while the
  same two garments bought separately read BAG [2]. Same parcel, different
  number. This expands bundle lines into their components so the count means
  one thing everywhere.

  Rendered bare (no markup) so it can be both interpolated into the header and
  served on its own by templates/cart.crk-count.liquid, which is what the
  JavaScript refetches after an add. One rule, one place.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign crk_bag_n = 0
  for crk_line in cart.items
    if crk_line.item_components.size > 0
      for crk_comp in crk_line.item_components
        assign crk_bag_n = crk_bag_n | plus: crk_comp.quantity
      endfor
    else
      assign crk_bag_n = crk_bag_n | plus: crk_line.quantity
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{{- crk_bag_n -}}
